72.551912568306,"to_t":2006.9506849315069,"title":"King of Bhutan","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Jigme Singye Wangchuck"},{"qid":"Q917","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q298020","value_label":"Jigme Dorji Wangchuck","from_t":1952.8196721311476,"to_t":1972.551912568306,"title":"King of Bhutan","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Jigme Dorji Wangchuck"},{"qid":"Q917","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q318177","value_label":"Jigme Wangchuck","from_t":1926.6356164383562,"to_t":1952.2431693989072,"title":"King of Bhutan","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Jigme Wangchuck"},{"qid":"Q917","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q333866","value_label":"Ugyen Wangchuck","from_t":1907.958904109589,"to_t":1926.6356164383562,"title":"King of Bhutan","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Ugyen Wangchuck"},{"qid":"Q917","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q57376","value_label":"Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck","from_t":2006.9506849315069,"to_t":null,"title":"King of Bhutan","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck"},{"qid":"Q917","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q134521","value_label":"Flag of Bhutan.svg","from_t":1969,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Bhutan","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Bhutan"}],"people":{"Q57376":{"label":"Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck","description":"fifth and reigning King of Bhutan","enwiki":"Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck","summary":"Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck (born 21 February 1980) is the current King of Bhutan, reigning since 9 December 2006. A member of the Wangchuck dynasty, he is the eldest son of King Jigme Singye Wangchuck, and his third wife, Queen Tshering Yangdon. He received his early education in Bhutan before studying abroad in the United States and the United Kingdom, ultimately graduating from Wheaton College with a degree in politics.\nHis father abdicated the throne on 14 December 2006 after 34 years of rule, making Jigme Khesar the world's youngest reigning monarch at the time, aged 26.","image":"Prime Minister of Bharat Shri Narendra Damodardas Modi with Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck and Jetsun Pema (cropped).jpg","birth":1980.139344262295,"death":null},"Q7849613":{"label":"Tshering Tobgay","description":"7th Prime Minister of Bhutan","enwiki":"Tshering Tobgay","summary":"Tshering Tobgay (born 19 September 1965) is a Bhutanese politician who is the seventh prime minister of Bhutan since 2024, having previously held the office from 2013 to 2018. Tobgay is the leader of the People's Democratic Party, and was also the Leader of the Opposition in the National Assembly from March 2008 to April 2013.","image":"Tshering Tobgay.jpg","birth":1965.7150684931507,"death":null},"Q200273":{"label":"Jigme Singye Wangchuck","description":"King of Bhutan from 1972–2006","enwiki":"Jigme Singye Wangchuck","summary":"Jigme Singye Wangchuck (Dzongkha: འཇིགས་མེད་སེང་གེ་དབང་ཕྱུག་, Wylie: jigs med seng ge dbang phyug; born 11 November 1955) is a member of the Wangchuck dynasty who reigned as King of Bhutan from 1972 until his abdication in 2006. He is the father of the present King Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck. He is the only son of five children born to the King Jigme Dorji Wangchuck and Queen Ashi Kesang Choden.\nJigme Singye Wangchuck studied at St.","image":"Jigme Singye Wangchuck on November 12, 2025 (cropped).jpg","birth":1955.8602739726027,"death":null},"Q298020":{"label":"Jigme Dorji Wangchuck","description":"King of Bhutan (1929-1972)","enwiki":"Jigme Dorji Wangchuck","summary":"Jigme Dorji Wangchuck (Dzongkha: འབྲུག་རྒྱལ་པོ་ འཇིགས་མེད་རྡོ་རྗེ་དབང་ཕྱུག་མཆོག་, Wylie: 'brug rgyal po 'jigs med rdo rje dbang phyug mchog; 2 May 1928 – 21 July 1972) was King of Bhutan from 30 March 1952 until his death in 1972.\nHe began to open Bhutan to the outside world, began modernization, and took the first step towards democratization.","image":"50 Ngultrum Vorderseite.jpg","birth":1929.331506849315,"death":1972.551912568306},"Q318177":{"label":"Jigme Wangchuck","description":"King of Bhutan (1906-1952)","enwiki":"Jigme Wangchuck","summary":"Jigme Wangchuck (Dzongkha: འཇིགས་མེད་དབང་ཕྱུག, Wylie: ’jigs med dbang phyug; 1905 – 30 March 1952) was King of Bhutan from 26 August 1926 until his death in 1952. He pursued legal and infrastructural reform during his reign. Bhutan continued to maintain almost complete isolation from the outside world during this period; its only foreign relations were with the British Raj in India, under which Bhutan was a protected state. He was succeeded by his son, Jigme Dorji Wangchuck.","image":"Bhutan-Jigme-Wangchuck.jpg","birth":1906,"death":1952.2431693989072},"Q333866":{"label":"Ugyen Wangchuck","description":"king of Bhutan (1862-1926)","enwiki":"Ugyen Wangchuck","summary":"Gongsar Ugyen Wangchuck (Dzongkha: ཨོ་རྒྱན་དབང་ཕྱུག, Wylie: o rgyan dbang phyug; 11 June 1862 – 26 August 1926) was the founder and first king of Bhutan, reigning from 17 December 1907 until his death in 1926. In his lifetime, he made efforts to unite the fledgling country.","image":"Ugyen Wangchuck, 1905.jpg","birth":1862.441095890411,"death":1926.6356164383562}},"media":{"Flag of Bhutan.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Flag_of_Bhutan.svg/330px-Flag_of_Bhutan.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bhutan.svg","author":"See File history below for details.","license":"Public domain"},"Emblem of Bhutan.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Emblem_of_Bhutan.svg/330px-Emblem_of_Bhutan.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_Bhutan.svg","author":"Original Author: Vector-Images.com\nConverted to SVG by: Oren neu dag","license":"Public domain"},"Prime Minister of Bharat Shri Narendra Damodardas Modi with Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck and Jetsun Pema (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Prime_Minister_of_Bharat_Shri_Narendra_Damodardas_Modi_with_Jigme_Khesar_Namgyel_Wangchuck_and_Jetsun_Pema_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prime_Minister_of_Bharat_Shri_Narendra_Damodardas_Modi_with_Jigme_Khesar_Namgyel_Wangchuck_and_Jetsun_Pema_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_of_Bharat_Shri_Narendra_Damodardas_Modi_with_Jigme_Khesar_Namgyel_Wangchuck_and_Jetsun_Pema_(cropped).jpg","author":"Prime Minister's Office","license":"GODL-India"},"Tshering Tobgay.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Tshering_Tobgay.jpg/330px-Tshering_Tobgay.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tshering_Tobgay.jpg","author":"Tshering Tobgay","license":"CC BY 3.0"},"Jigme Singye Wangchuck on November 12, 2025 (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Jigme_Singye_Wangchuck_on_November_12%2C_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Jigme_Singye_Wangchuck_on_November_12%2C_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jigme_Singye_Wangchuck_on_November_12,_2025_(cropped).jpg","author":"Prime Minister's Office","license":"GODL-India"},"50 Ngultrum Vorderseite.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/50_Ngultrum_Vorderseite.jpg/330px-50_Ngultrum_Vorderseite.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:50_Ngultrum_Vorderseite.jpg","author":null,"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"Bhutan-Jigme-Wangchuck.jpg":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f3/Bhutan-Jigme-Wangchuck.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_ca